{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Mama said don't go [C]near that river
[G]Don't be hanging around old Catfish [D]John
[G]But come the morning I'd [C]always be there
[G]Walking in his footsteps in the [D]sweet delta [G]dawn
Take me [C]back, to another [G]moment
To a [C]time, so long [G]ago
When the [C]sweet, magnolias [G]blossomed
The cotton [G]fields,  [D]were white as [G]snow
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Catfish John was a river hobo
He lived and died, by the rivers bend
Looking back, I still remember
I was proud,   to be his friend
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
Born a slave, in the town of Vicksburg
Traded for, a chestnut mare
Lord he never, spoke in anger
Though his load,   was hard to bear
{end_of_chorus}
